{"post_stream": {"posts": [{"id": 264927, "name": "NAVras", "username": "navras", "avatar_template": "https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/n/afea85/{size}.png", "created_at": "2023-12-24T17:38:04.550Z", "cooked": "<blockquote>\n<p>dnf mark group &lt;package-spec&gt;…<br>\nMarks the specified packages as installed by group. This can be useful if any package was installed as a dependency or a user and is desired to be protected and <strong>handled as a group member like during group remove</strong>.<sup class=\"footnote-ref\"><a href=\"#footnote-264927-1\" id=\"footnote-ref-264927-1\">[1]</a></sup></p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>However after my saga on trying to understand the group mark <sup class=\"footnote-ref\"><a href=\"#footnote-264927-2\" id=\"footnote-ref-264927-2\">[2]</a></sup>, I’m kinda convinced that this is broken (or doesn’t do what it says).</p>\n<pre><code class=\"lang-plaintext\">$ dnf repoquery --whatdepends flatpak --installed\nfedora-flathub-remote-0:1-6.fc39.noarch\ngnome-software-0:45.2-1.fc39.x86_64\n$ sudo dnf remove fedora-flathub-remote\n$ sudo dnf remove gnome-software\n# Wants to remove flatpak, cancelled.\n\n$ dnf repoquery --groupmember flatpak\nflatpak-1.15.6-1.fc39.x86_64\n  @container-management\n# Fedora Workstation has container-management by default.\n$ sudo dnf mark group flatpak\n$ sudo dnf remove gnome-software\n# Does not remove flatpak, good.\n\n$ sudo dnf group remove container-management\n# Does not want to remove flatpak, what?!\n\n# Checking\n$ dnf repoquery --whatdepends flatpak --installed\n# Nothing\n$ dnf repoquery --installed --qf='%{name}-%{evr}.%{arch} (%{reason})' flatpak\nflatpak-1.15.6-1.fc39.x86_64 (group)\n</code></pre>\n<hr class=\"footnotes-sep\">\n\n<ol class=\"footnotes-list\">\n<li id=\"footnote-264927-1\" class=\"footnote-item\"><p><a href=\"https://dnf.readthedocs.io/en/latest/command_ref.html#mark-command\" class=\"onebox\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">https://dnf.readthedocs.io/en/latest/command_ref.html#mark-command</a> <a href=\"#footnote-ref-264927-1\" class=\"footnote-backref\">↩︎</a></p>\n</li>\n<li id=\"footnote-264927-2\" class=\"footnote-item\"><p><a href=\"https://discussion.fedoraproject.org/t/find-in-which-group-the-package-was-installed/96601\">1</a> <a href=\"https://discussion.fedoraproject.org/t/verify-dnf-group-marks/96615\">2</a> <a href=\"https://discussion.fedoraproject.org/t/remove-the-explicit-dnf-mark-on-container-management/100179\">3</a> <a href=\"#footnote-ref-264927-2\" class=\"footnote-backref\">↩︎</a></p>\n</li>\n</ol>", "post_number": 1, "post_type": 1, "posts_count": 3, "updated_at": "2023-12-24T17:38:04.550Z", "reply_count": 0, "reply_to_post_number": null, "quote_count": 0, "incoming_link_count": 183, "reads": 17, "readers_count": 16, "score": 918.4, "yours": false, "topic_id": 100181, "topic_slug": "dnf-mark-group-doesnt-make-package-part-of-a-group", "display_username": "NAVras", "primary_group_name": null, "flair_name": null, "flair_url": null, "flair_bg_color": null, "flair_color": null, "flair_group_id": null, "badges_granted": [], "version": 1, "can_edit": false, "can_delete": false, "can_recover": false, "can_see_hidden_post": false, "can_wiki": false, "link_counts": [{"url": "https://dnf.readthedocs.io/en/latest/command_ref.html#mark-command", "internal": false, "reflection": false, "title": "DNF Command Reference — dnf latest documentation", "clicks": 2}, {"url": "https://discussion.fedoraproject.org/t/find-in-which-group-the-package-was-installed/96601", "internal": true, "reflection": false, "title": "Find in which group the package was installed", "clicks": 0}, {"url": "https://discussion.fedoraproject.org/t/verify-dnf-group-marks/96615", "internal": true, "reflection": false, "title": "Verify dnf group marks", "clicks": 0}, {"url": "https://discussion.fedoraproject.org/t/remove-the-explicit-dnf-mark-on-container-management/100179", "internal": true, "reflection": false, "title": "Remove the explicit dnf mark on \"Container Management\"", "clicks": 0}], "read": true, "user_title": "", "bookmarked": false, "actions_summary": [], "moderator": false, "admin": false, "staff": false, "user_id": 4817, "hidden": false, "trust_level": 2, "deleted_at": null, "user_deleted": false, "edit_reason": null, "can_view_edit_history": true, "wiki": false, "mentioned_users": [], "post_url": "/t/dnf-mark-group-doesnt-make-package-part-of-a-group/100181/1", "event": null, "calendar_details": [], "reactions": [], "current_user_reaction": null, "reaction_users_count": 0, "current_user_used_main_reaction": false, "can_accept_answer": false, "can_unaccept_answer": false, "accepted_answer": false, "topic_accepted_answer": true}, {"id": 264945, "name": "Chris Williams", "username": "chrisawi", "avatar_template": "https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/c/eb7434/{size}.png", "created_at": "2023-12-24T20:18:58.572Z", "cooked": "<p>This is the first I’ve heard of <code>dnf mark group</code>, but maybe it’s because flatpak is only an optional member of that group.</p>", "post_number": 2, "post_type": 1, "posts_count": 3, "updated_at": "2023-12-24T20:18:58.572Z", "reply_count": 0, "reply_to_post_number": null, "quote_count": 0, "incoming_link_count": 0, "reads": 15, "readers_count": 14, "score": 18.0, "yours": false, "topic_id": 100181, "topic_slug": "dnf-mark-group-doesnt-make-package-part-of-a-group", "display_username": "Chris Williams", "primary_group_name": null, "flair_name": null, "flair_url": null, "flair_bg_color": null, "flair_color": null, "flair_group_id": null, "badges_granted": [], "version": 1, "can_edit": false, "can_delete": false, "can_recover": false, "can_see_hidden_post": false, "can_wiki": false, "read": true, "user_title": null, "bookmarked": false, "actions_summary": [{"id": 2, "count": 1}], "moderator": false, "admin": false, "staff": false, "user_id": 16855, "hidden": false, "trust_level": 2, "deleted_at": null, "user_deleted": false, "edit_reason": null, "can_view_edit_history": true, "wiki": false, "mentioned_users": [], "post_url": "/t/dnf-mark-group-doesnt-make-package-part-of-a-group/100181/2", "event": null, "reactions": [{"id": "heart", "type": "emoji", "count": 1}], "current_user_reaction": null, "reaction_users_count": 1, "current_user_used_main_reaction": false, "can_accept_answer": false, "can_unaccept_answer": false, "accepted_answer": false, "topic_accepted_answer": true}, {"id": 264963, "name": "NAVras", "username": "navras", "avatar_template": "https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/n/afea85/{size}.png", "created_at": "2023-12-25T03:09:30.104Z", "cooked": "<p>I tried it on a Live USB and it works as expected:</p>\n<pre><code class=\"lang-plaintext\">$ sudo dnf mark group flatpak\n$ sudo dnf remove fedora-flathub-remote gnome-software\n$ sudo dnf remove @container-management\n# See flatpak in the remove list.\n</code></pre>\n<p>I think what happened was that I used <code>sudo dnf group mark remove container-management</code> before, which irrecoverably made those packages orphaned.</p>\n<pre><code class=\"lang-plaintext\">$ sudo dnf group mark remove container-management\n$ sudo dnf group install container-management\n$ sudo dnf group remove container-management\n# Nothing in the list!\n# Try everything, but it will never work again...\n</code></pre>\n<p>EDIT:<br>\n<code>sudo dnf group install container-management --with-optional</code> can fix it, but will need to install all optional packages.</p>", "post_number": 3, "post_type": 1, "posts_count": 3, "updated_at": "2023-12-25T03:40:11.204Z", "reply_count": 0, "reply_to_post_number": null, "quote_count": 0, "incoming_link_count": 4, "reads": 12, "readers_count": 11, "score": 22.4, "yours": false, "topic_id": 100181, "topic_slug": "dnf-mark-group-doesnt-make-package-part-of-a-group", "display_username": "NAVras", "primary_group_name": null, "flair_name": null, "flair_url": null, "flair_bg_color": null, "flair_color": null, "flair_group_id": null, "badges_g